    {
      "page": "model",
      "label": "model-figure-1",
      "source_block_id": "40025656-1ff8-80cf-a873-c4d74bc54627",
      "caption": "Figure 1. The complete neural network. An odor (Odor A) enters the sensory unit (PN), is projected onto the coding unit (KC), and the output unit (MBON) gives the answer. Red neurons are global regulators: ALLN activation and inhibition at the PN layer, APL inhibition at the KC layer, and global inhibition at the MBON layer. The forced answer on the right is the teacher signal used during training. The experiments on this page use PN, KC, APL, MBON, MBON global inhibition and the forced answer; the RPE (DAN) and ALLN neurons drawn in the figure are not part of the model used here.",
      "sha256": "9b14ea300c0fa76df4a4a575f1d1591072e894a68db7cbaf8fe0562d44cdf369",
      "bytes": 45080,
